  "semanticBug": {
    "cause": "SetIdxF performed raw stores; generic and integer stores required an own metatable before checking declaration-based __newindex. Threaded and native integer array fast paths treated nil holes as occupied.",
    "repair": "Semantic SetIdx, SetIdxF and SetIdxI dispatch through newindex, which resolves own metatables and record declarations for absent keys. Threaded and native inline array stores send interceptable holes to the helper. The compiled integer helper roots its exact key in a guarded handle scope so handler errors unwind it.",
    "preserved": [
      "Occupied keys use raw stores; rawset and set_index retain raw semantics.",
      "Table handlers, handler replacement, reentry, GC and handler errors preserve their contracts.",
      "Sparse maps retain fractional, absent and exact wide integer keys; raw maps reject nil and NaN keys.",
      "Integer-indexed shapes remain sparse maps with optional reads and do not fit dense {T} arrays."
    ],
    "publicSymptoms": "Fractional GPU Shared writes bypassed validation; negative provider-array writes bypassed bounds; storage-view float-indexed writes made shadow table entries instead of updating backing bytes used by bitset copy and fill."
  },
